treekipedia:AngMaFaFbCx09076-00 tkp:culturalSignificance "As an Australian Acacia (wattle), this species belongs to a genus with 50,000+ years of cultural significance to Aboriginal peoples. Wattles have been used traditionally for food (seeds, gum), medicine (bark infusions, antiseptic gum), tools, and as seasonal indicators. The Golden Wattle is Australia national floral emblem." .
