treekipedia:AngMaFaFbCx09076-00 tkp:identification_features "Distinguished by: (1) Long linear phyllodes 6-19 cm tapering to apex; (2) Creamy yellow globular flower heads in 10-16-headed racemes; (3) Spindly glabrous habit 2-8m tall; (4) Gland positioned 10-30mm above pulvinus. Differs from A. adunca by creamy (not golden) flowers and thinner phyllodes." .
