treekipedia:AngMaFaFbCx09077-01 tkp:culturalSignificance "Highly valued by Noongar/Nyungar people of Western Australia for wood, food, and medicine. Seeds (45% protein) were ground into flour. Edible orange gum/resin used for food and tea. Wood used for implements and weapons. One of the most culturally significant Acacias in south-west Western Australia." .
