treekipedia:AngMaFaFbCx09077-01 tkp:generalDescription "Acacia acuminata is a tall shrub or small tree 3-7m (up to 10m) high with an obconic form (narrower at base). Endemic to south-west Western Australia, it is recognized for its distinctive raspberry jam scent when the wood is cut. It has bright green linear phyllodes and produces golden-yellow flower spikes from July to October." .
