treekipedia:AngMaFaFbCx09077-01 tkp:pruningMaintenance "Can be hedged by harsh pruning to maintain any desired height. Best pruned in late winter to early spring before new growth. Established specimens need only minimal pruning for dead, diseased or misplaced branches. Pruning improves air circulation and reduces fungal disease risk." .
