treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:barkCharacteristics "Thin (notably thinner than other Trans-Pecos oaks at all trunk diameters). Color: Light brown to grayish-brown. Texture: Papery, flaky, smooth on young stems. Does not develop thick, furrowed bark with age like many other oaks. The thin bark reflects fire survival strategy based on resprouting rather than bark protection." .
