treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:ecologicalFunction "Wildlife food source: Acorns eaten by birds, javelinas, mule deer, bighorn sheep, and various small mammals. Keystone species for insects: Hosts numerous insects that support insectivorous birds. Erosion control: Thicket-forming growth stabilizes rocky slopes. Nurse plant: Provides microhabitat and shade for other species establishment. Hybridization: Genetic exchange with gray oak (Q. grisea) in Guadalupe Mountains contributes to oak diversity." .
