treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:etymology "Genus name Quercus is Latin for oak. Species name pungens means spiny or sharp-pointed in Latin, referring to the spinose-tipped leaf lobes. The common name Sandpaper Oak refers to the rough, sandpapery texture of the leaves caused by minute persistent hair bases on both leaf surfaces." .
