treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:fireManagement "Fire ecology: Relies entirely on resprouting for fire survival; thin bark provides minimal protection. Post-fire response: Sprouts prolifically from root crown following top-kill. Post-fire community: May become denser than pre-fire due to vigorous sprouting. Recovery: All Arizona oaks, including Q. pungens, sprout prolifically after fire. Management: Allow natural fire regime; species adapted to mixed fire regime of Chihuahuan Desert Sky Islands." .
