treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:fruitType "Acorn (nut). Size: Small, up to 13mm (0.5 inch) long. Shape: Ovoid. Color: Chestnut-brown (nut), light brown (shell). Cup: Top-shaped with gray pubescence, enclosing approximately 1/4 of nut. Arrangement: Solitary or paired, sessile or on very short stalks (peduncle up to 3mm). Maturation: Annual (matures in one season - white oak group characteristic)." .
