treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:generalDescription "Quercus pungens is a North American evergreen to semi-evergreen shrub or small tree in the white oak group (section Quercus), native to the southwestern United States and northeastern Mexico. Typically growing as a multi-stemmed shrub 1-3m tall or occasionally as a small tree to 8-12m, it is characterized by small, leathery leaves with a distinctive rough, sandpapery texture. The species is adapted to dry, rocky slopes in chaparral, desert scrub, and oak-juniper-pinyon woodland communities." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_f895e693-3c03-4eb3-b401-51f2a7671db1> a tkp:Insight ;
