treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:growthForm "Evergreen to semi-evergreen (subevergreen) shrub or small tree. Typically shrubby: 1-3m (3-10 ft) tall, much-branched from base, forming thickets. Tree form: Up to 8-12m (26-39 ft) in favorable sites, occasionally reaching 12m. Growth habit varies with site conditions: shrubby on exposed, dry sites; more tree-like in protected canyons. Multi-stemmed growth common. White oak group member." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_7155b6fe-e1ec-42c2-9205-98184b4a0bf8> a tkp:Insight ;
