treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 dwc:habitat "Dry limestone or igneous slopes in chaparral, desert scrub savanna, and oak-juniper-pinyon woodlands. Found at elevations of 800-2000m (2600-6600 ft). Occurs on middle to upper slopes and in lower canyons of desert mountains, along arroyos. Associated with thin, rocky soils in semiarid to subhumid climates with hot summers and mild winters. Characteristic of juniper-oak communities in Edwards Plateau and Trans-Pecos Texas, Sky Island mountain ranges, and northeastern Mexico." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_e82def49-bb3e-4080-a450-050543711ba4> a tkp:Insight ;
