treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:identification_features "Evergreen to semi-evergreen shrub or small tree. Leaves small (10-19mm wide), elliptic to oblong, thick and leathery, with wavy margins and coarse teeth or spinose lobes; distinctive sandpapery texture on both surfaces from minute hair bases; shiny yellowish-green above, densely pubescent beneath. Bark thin, light brown, papery and flaky. Twigs gray with velvety hairs when young. Acorns small (up to 13mm), annual, sessile or short-stalked, with cup enclosing 1/4 of nut." .
