treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:leafType "Simple, alternate. Size: Small, 10-19mm wide (among smallest oak leaves). Shape: Elliptic to oblong. Margins: Wavy, with coarse teeth or spinose lobes. Apex: Acute or obtuse with mucronate (spine-tipped) tip. Base: Rounded. Texture: Thick, leathery, sandpapery on both surfaces from minute persistent hair bases. Color: Shiny yellowish-green above, dense pubescence beneath. Petiole: Short, up to 10mm." .
