treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 dwc:measurementValue "Typical shrub form: 1-3 meters (3-10 feet). Tree form: Up to 8 meters (26 feet) commonly; maximum 12 meters (39 feet) in exceptional circumstances. Usually shrubby: Rarely exceeds head height on exposed limestone hilltops. Height varies greatly with site conditions and moisture availability." .
