treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:maximumTreeAge "No documented maximum age for Quercus pungens. Given its fire-adapted, resprouting nature, individual aboveground stems are likely replaced periodically while root crowns persist much longer. Clonal root systems could potentially be centuries old even when stems are younger." .
