treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:nonTimberProducts "Acorns: Edible after processing to remove tannins; wildlife food. Bark/galls: Source of tannins for traditional medicine (astringent, antibacterial). Fuel: Firewood for local use. Wildlife value: Acorn mast crop important for game animals. Ornamental: Native landscaping, xeriscaping, bonsai potential due to interesting shrubby form." .
