treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:nutritional_caloric_value "Acorns: Edible after leaching to remove tannins. Nutritional content: High in carbohydrates (starch), moderate fat and protein (typical of white oak group acorns). Processing required: Tannins must be leached by soaking in water or burial in wet soil. Uses: Ground into flour or meal after processing. White oak group acorns generally lower in tannins than red oak group, but still require processing." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_6330cca3-c4fb-4ec2-870d-82ae90f253c6> a tkp:Insight ;
