treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:plantingRecipes "Seed collection: Collect acorns when brown and falling naturally (autumn). Sow immediately: Acorns lose viability quickly in storage. Planting depth: Plant 2-3cm deep in well-drained medium. Container: Use deep containers to accommodate taproot development. Protection: Cover outdoor beds with wire mesh to prevent rodent predation. Soil: Sandy or gravelly, well-drained mix; can add limestone gravel. No stratification required (white oak group)." .
