treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:stewardshipPractices "Site selection: Plant on well-drained, rocky or gravelly soils; limestone preferred. Sun exposure: Full sun required. Watering: Drought-tolerant once established; avoid overwatering. Climate: Best in regions with hot summers and mild winters. Fire management: Allow natural fire regime; species recovers through resprouting. Protection: Exclude livestock grazing in restoration areas to allow establishment." .
