treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14878-00 tkp:timberValue "Commercial timber value: Very low to none. Size limitation: Rarely grows large enough for timber use. Wood: Dense and hard (typical of oaks) but stems too small for lumber. Local uses: Fuel wood (firewood, charcoal), fence posts. The oaks of Arizona including Q. pungens are described as rarely growing large enough for timber use." .
