treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:agroforestryUses "Dehesa/Montado systems: Traditional agrosilvopastoral system in Iberian Peninsula incorporating Q. pyrenaica alongside Q. ilex and Q. suber. Livestock integration: Cattle, sheep, and Iberian pigs graze beneath oaks; acorns provide autumn forage (montanera). Silvopasture: Grazing controls understory vegetation, reduces fire risk, supports biodiversity. Carbon sequestration: Secondary forests accumulate substantial biomass within decades. Products: Firewood, charcoal, grazing, cork (in mixed stands), honey, mushrooms." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_527a9cbd-45ba-4e60-b0fa-7f230ff0b174> a tkp:Insight ;
