treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:climate_tolerance "Temperature: Mean annual 6-15°C; tolerates winter cold to -5°C and summer heat to 22°C. Southern populations tolerate hotter conditions with compensatory rainfall. Precipitation: Requires sufficient annual rainfall, especially summer moisture; precipitation is main driver of habitat suitability. Adapted to pronounced dry season through marcescence and short growth season. Vulnerable to increasing drought severity and heatwaves under climate change." .
