treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:compatibleSoilTypes "Strongly prefers siliceous, acidic soils (pH 4.5-6.5). Typical substrates include schists, quartzites, and granite-derived soils. Dominant soil texture is sandy-loam with some clayey-loam presence. Primary soil types: Umbric Regosols, Cambisols, Leptosols. Oligotrophic (nutrient-poor) soils are characteristic. Occasionally found on limestone or dolomite but not preferred. Requires well-drained conditions." .
