treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:culturalSignificance "Traditional importance in Iberian rural economy for firewood, charcoal production, and livestock grazing (dehesa/montado silvopastoral systems). Historical use of bark tannins for leather production. Acorns historically consumed by humans during food scarcity (requires tannin removal). Oak veneration in pre-Christian Celtic and Indo-European traditions; sacred to thunder gods (Zeus, Thor, Perkūnas). Celtic priests (druids) etymologically connected to oak. In Galicia (NW Spain), sacred landscapes incorporate oak groves with later Christian overlay." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_d9a816aa-2081-42d7-a9a3-2eb1e6460f35> a tkp:Insight ;
