treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:diseasePestManagement "Key pests: Green oak leaf roller moth (Tortrix viridana), gypsy moth (Lymantria dispar), brown-tail moth (Euproctis chrysorrhoea), two-spotted oak buprestid beetle (Agrilus biguttatus). Diseases: Acute Oak Decline (AOD) bacteria documented in Spain; Phytophthora species causing root rot; powdery mildew. Management: Monitor for defoliators; promote tree vigor through appropriate thinning; avoid waterlogging that favors Phytophthora; maintain stand health to resist beetle attacks." .
