treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:ecologicalFunction "Dominant keystone species forming closed-canopy forest ecosystems. Provides critical food source (acorns) for wildlife including squirrels, deer, wild boar, and numerous bird species. Dense foliage offers shelter and nesting sites for birds. Supports rich understory communities of heaths (Erica spp.) and brooms (Cytisus spp.). Important for soil and water conservation. Provides habitat for the endangered Cantabrian Capercaillie at its southernmost range. Supports diverse mycorrhizal communities. Leaf litter rich in tannins affects soil chemistry and nutrient cycling." .
