treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:etymology "The genus name Quercus is Latin for oak, with possible Celtic origins meaning beautiful tree. The specific epithet pyrenaica refers to the Pyrenees mountains, though this was a mistake by botanist Carl Ludwig von Willdenow who named it based on dry samples received with an incorrect label indicating Pyrenean origin." .
