treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:fireManagement "Fire ecology: Species exhibits one of most vigorous resprouting responses in genus Quercus; regenerates primarily from root crown and rhizome sprouts after fire. Low seed germination after fire but ecosystem adapted to periodic burning. Post-fire recovery: Rapid vegetative recovery; clonal regeneration exceeds 80% in some plots. Fire management: Reduce fuel loads through thinning; traditional grazing helps control understory vegetation; multi-stemmed resprout stands highly flammable - consider fuel breaks. Recovery time: Structural recovery takes 15+ years." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_dc05d7a7-066b-4c08-b279-c24f4ba0f561> a tkp:Insight ;
