treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:fruitType "Acorn (nut). Thick, ovoid to ellipsoid, 2-3 cm long. Green when immature, turning brown when ripe. Produced 2-4 together on erect, downy stalks (1-4 cm). Cup (cupule) hemispherical, covering about half the acorn, with appressed downy scales. Matures in first year (annual fruiting). Dispersed by birds and small mammals including jays, squirrels, and wild boar." .
