treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:generalDescription "Quercus pyrenaica is a medium-sized deciduous oak native to southwestern Europe and northwestern Morocco. It is a marcescent species (retaining dead leaves through winter), growing 15-25m tall with an irregular, wide crown. An intermediate species between temperate and Mediterranean oaks, it is adapted to hot, dry summers with a short growth season. The species is characterized by deeply lobed, velvety leaves that emerge pinkish, turn deep green in summer, and become yellowish-brown in autumn before persisting through winter." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_548303ec-9d59-47b3-be79-2896a9a55edd> a tkp:Insight ;
