treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:growthForm "Medium-sized deciduous tree, occasionally shrubby. Single or multi-stemmed depending on management history. Typically 15-25m tall, occasionally reaching 30m. Irregular, wide, much-branched crown. Slender trunk, often tortuous. Strong tendency to produce root suckers and basal sprouts. Marcescent habit (retaining dead leaves through winter, especially in immature individuals)." .
