treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 dwc:habitat "Mid-mountain forests on siliceous, acidic soils in transitional zones between temperate deciduous and Mediterranean sclerophyllous ecosystems. Found from sea level to 2,100m elevation. Grows in Atlantic-Mediterranean regions with humid to hyperhumid supramediterranean conditions. Forms closed-canopy stands as a dominant species. In Iberia, occupies approximately 660,000 hectares in Spain and 81,700 hectares in Portugal." .
