treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:maximumDiameter "Trunk diameter typically 40-80 cm DBH in mature trees. Often slender and tortuous, limiting timber utility compared to Q. robur or Q. petraea. Multi-stemmed coppice stools may have individual stems of 20-40 cm diameter. Record specimens may exceed 100 cm DBH." .
