treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:nativeHabitats "Native to southwestern Europe: Spain (primary range, 660,000 ha), Portugal (81,700 ha), western France, and northern Morocco. Adapted to Atlantic-Mediterranean transitional climates with mean annual temperatures 6-15°C. Thrives in humid to hyperhumid supramediterranean conditions. Siliceous substrate specialist but occasionally found on limestone. Climate zones: Köppen Csb (warm-summer Mediterranean) to Cfb (oceanic)." .
