treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:nonTimberProducts "Tannins: Bark and galls rich in tannins for leather tanning and traditional medicine (astringent). Fodder: Leaves historically used as green fodder for cattle. Acorns: Wildlife food; historically human food (requires leaching). Charcoal: High-quality charcoal production from coppiced wood. Honey: Nectar source for beekeeping. Mushrooms: Host for edible mycorrhizal fungi. Dyes: Tannins provide brown dyes. Cork: Not produced (unlike Q. suber), but mixed stands may include cork oaks." .
