treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:nutritional_caloric_value "Acorns: Rich in carbohydrates (starch content ~19%); lipids high in oleic acid (42%) and linoleic acid (34%); significant protein content; minerals including potassium, calcium, iron. High tannin content requires processing (leaching, boiling, or burial) before human consumption. Traditional processing: Burial in boggy ground to leach tannins; wrapping in cloth in running water. Modern uses: Gluten-free flour for bread; roasted as coffee substitute. Primarily used as livestock and wildlife feed." .
