treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:plantingRecipes "Site selection: Acidic, siliceous, well-drained soils; mid-elevation slopes (400-1600m); temperate to sub-Mediterranean climate. Seed treatment: Collect ripe acorns in autumn; sow immediately or store moist and cool; stratify for 2-3 months if spring planting. Sowing: Direct sow 2-3 cm deep in autumn, or plant 1-year seedlings. Spacing: 3-4m for forest planting. Protection: Tree guards essential against browsing; mulch to retain moisture. First years: Keep soil moist but not waterlogged; remove competing vegetation." .
