treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:propagation_methods "Sexual (seed): Collect ripe acorns autumn; sow immediately (seeds lose viability quickly if dried); protect from rodents; stratify 60-90 days if storing; germination in spring. Vegetative: Root cuttings possible but challenging; layering; natural root suckering prolific (species produces abundant suckers). Clonal propagation: >80% of regeneration in some stands is clonal. Grafting: Standard methods for oaks applicable." .
