treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:pruningMaintenance "Timing: Prune during dormant season (late winter) to minimize disease transmission. For coppice conversion: Remove competing stems, retain 1-3 best stems per stool. Thinning: Remove 25-35% of basal area for moderate thinning; up to 50% for intensive thinning to promote growth. Remove dead, diseased, or crossing branches. Avoid heavy pruning that creates large wounds. Historical coppice rotation: 7-20 years for firewood production." .
