treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:stewardshipPractices "For established forests: Convert abandoned coppices to high forest through selective thinning (25-50% basal area removal). Avoid intense thinning that removes unique genotypes. Maintain genetic diversity by preserving trees of different age classes. For restoration: Plant on acidic, siliceous soils. Protect from browsing animals with tree guards. Use local seed sources. For fire management: Thin stands to reduce fuel loads and fire risk. Maintain structural heterogeneity through traditional practices like grazing." .
