treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:timberValue "Wood properties: Heavy, hard, tough, durable; density approximately 0.75 g/cm³ (700-900 kg/m³ for oaks generally). Quality: Considered inferior to Q. robur and Q. petraea due to irregular, tortuous trunk limiting board quality. Uses: Poles, railway sleepers (ties), rustic carpentry, furniture, cooperage (wine barrel aging), flooring. Firewood: Excellent fuel, burns well with good heat output. Charcoal: Produces high-quality charcoal. Primary traditional use was coppice for firewood rather than timber production." .
