treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14880-00 tkp:tolerances "Drought: Moderate tolerance; more drought-tolerant than Pinus sylvestris at elevational boundaries, shows no significant vessel diameter change under drought stress. Fire: Excellent resprouting ability from root crown and rhizomes; one of most vigorous resprouters in genus Quercus. Shade: Moderate tolerance in juvenile stage. Wind: Moderate tolerance. Frost: Hardy to USDA Zone 7 (-18°C). Salt: Not salt-tolerant. Waterlogging: Poor tolerance; requires well-drained soils." .
