treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:culturalSignificance "National emblem of England. Sacred to Zeus (Greece), Jupiter (Rome), Thor (Norse), and Celtic druids. Royal Oak commemorates Charles II hiding in Boscobel Oak (1651). Oak Apple Day (May 29) still celebrated. \"Royal Oak\" is third most common pub name in Britain. Featured on coins, coats of arms, National Trust emblem. Robin Hood legend at Major Oak." .
