treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:diseasePestManagement "Major threats: Acute Oak Decline (AOD) - bacterial infection with Agrilus beetle, can kill in 4-6 years, 80% mortality in some UK areas. Oak Processionary Moth (OPM) - defoliating caterpillars with irritating hairs. Powdery mildew (Erysiphe alphitoides) - foliar fungal disease, largely cosmetic. Monitor for stem lesions and bleeding (AOD symptoms)." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_ed956283-a19a-4c5b-874f-a604cd00e5ac> a tkp:Insight ;
