treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:ecologicalFunction "Keystone species supporting over 2,300 associated species in the UK. Provides critical habitat for insects (400+ herbivore species), birds, mammals, fungi, bryophytes, and lichens. Acorns are vital food source for squirrels, jays, deer, and wild boar. Old hollow trees provide roosting sites for bats and nesting sites for owls. Foundation species with disproportionate importance for biodiversity and ecosystem function." .
