treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:etymology "The genus name Quercus is the Latin name for oak trees. The species epithet robur is Latin meaning \"robust\" or \"strong\", referencing the strength and hardwood of this tree. Robur is an ancient Latin term for strong, hard wood, especially oak. Named by Carl Linnaeus in Species Plantarum (1753)." .
