treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:fruitType "Acorns (nuts) borne on long stalks (peduncles) 2-8cm - distinguishing feature from sessile oak. Acorns 2-2.5cm long, ovoid, ripening from green to brown in first autumn. Cup (cupule) covers about 1/4 of acorn with overlapping scales. Acorns mature in one growing season. Mast years (heavy production) occur irregularly." .
