treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:generalDescription "Quercus robur is a large, long-lived deciduous tree native to most of Europe west of the Caucasus. It is a keystone species in temperate broadleaf forests, supporting over 2,300 associated species in the UK alone. The tree is characterized by its broad spreading crown, deeply fissured bark, and iconic lobed leaves. It produces acorns on distinctive long stalks (peduncles) and can live for over 1,000 years." .
