treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 dwc:habitat "Found in deciduous and mixed woodlands, often forming dominant stands. Typical of valleys of large European rivers and damp lowlands. Pioneer species in plains and hills, late successional in valleys and floodplains. Common in lowland forests, wood pastures, coppice, and hedgerows. Tolerates intermittent flooding near swamps, rivers and ponds." .
