treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:identification_features "Distinguished by obovate leaves 10-12cm long with 4-5 rounded lobes on each side, very short petiole (2-7mm), distinctive auricles at leaf base. Acorns on long peduncles (2-8cm) - hence \"pedunculate oak\". Bark gray-brown with deep vertical fissures in mature trees. Crown broad and spreading with often twisted branches." .
