treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:maximumTreeAge "Some ancient oaks in Europe are estimated to be over 1,000-1,500 years old. The Bowthorpe Oak in Lincolnshire, England is estimated at 1,000+ years. Very durable wood even in decay stage contributes to longevity." .
