treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:nativeHabitats "Native to most of Europe and western Asia. Distribution includes all European countries from Ireland to the Caucasus, extending into Iran and Turkey. More typical of valleys and damp lowlands than sessile oak (Q. petraea). Adapted to temperate climate with warm summers and cool winters." .
