treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:nonTimberProducts "Tannins from bark for leather industry. Acorns historically used for pig fodder (pannage). Gall wasp galls produced oak gall ink. Cork (though primarily from Q. suber). Medicinal uses of bark (astringent). Dye from bark. Truffles associated with oak roots." .
