treekipedia:AngMaFaFgCx14888-00 tkp:nutritional_caloric_value "Acorns edible after leaching tannins. High in carbohydrates and fats. Historically important food source (acorn bread/flour) during famines. Raw acorns contain tannins that are toxic to humans but can be leached out. Acorns consumed by wildlife (deer, squirrels, jays, wild boar)." .
