treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:agroforestryUses "Traditional parkland agroforestry: Keystone tree in Sahelian parkland systems; ~2.8 million trees mapped in Sahel region. Intercropping: Grown with millet, sorghum, maize, groundnut, cowpea; effect on crop yield varies. Silvopasture: Compatible with cattle, goats, sheep grazing; provides shade and emergency fodder. Products harvested: Fruit (food, superfood powder export), leaves (vegetables, fodder), bark (fiber, medicine), seeds (oil). Carbon sequestration: Significant potential; parklands store ~1,284 Tg carbon at maximum coverage. Livelihood support: 94% of rural buildings in Senegal have baobab nearby; associated with better nutrition (dark leafy vegetable consumption). Domestication: Provenance trials show West African origins grow faster than East African." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_cb244329-b071-416d-9928-8fb72a0c89c3> a tkp:Insight ;
