treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:barkCharacteristics "Smooth, greyish to greyish-brown. Develops folds and seams with age, resembling elephant skin. Thickness: 5-10cm (2-4 inches), providing fire and drought protection. Inner bark (cambium): fibrous, reddish. Remarkable regeneration capacity: tree survives extensive bark stripping and regrows bark. Contains tannins (astringent). Spongy wood beneath bark stores water. Bark fiber traditionally harvested for rope, cloth, and basketry without killing tree." .
