treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 dwc:occurrenceStatus "IUCN Red List: Least Concern (LC) - widespread and locally common. However, protected as a national monument tree in South Africa. Faces increasing threats from: bark over-harvesting, fruit over-collection for superfood trade, climate change-induced drought, mining and development activities, mysterious die-offs of oldest specimens (cause unknown). Many largest, oldest trees (1000-2000+ years) have died in recent decades. Sooty baobab syndrome documented in drought-stressed populations." .
