treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:diseasePestManagement "Generally resistant to most pests and diseases due to thick bark and drought adaptations. Known pathogens: Lasiodiplodia theobromae (Botryosphaeriaceae fungus - potentially significant pathogen); root-knot nematodes (Meloidogyne sp.); reniform nematode (Rotylenchulus reniformis). Sooty baobab syndrome: Drought-induced, episodic condition causing blackened, dying appearance; linked to climate stress and human interference limiting soil moisture. Management: Maintain tree vigor; avoid waterlogging; sustainable harvesting to reduce stress; monitor for stem lesions and fungal infections." .
