treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:ecologicalFunction "Keystone species and ecosystem engineer creating micro-ecosystems. Water storage: massive trunk stores thousands of liters, vital for wildlife during droughts. Pollination: night-blooming flowers support fruit bat populations (80% of pollination). Seed dispersal: elephants and baboons are primary dispersers; passage through digestive tract aids germination. Nesting habitat: hollow trunks shelter African honey bees, birds, reptiles, and mammals. Nutrient cycling: deep roots access groundwater and minerals. Soil stabilization: prevents erosion in semi-arid landscapes. Food web: fruit, leaves, bark provide sustenance for elephants, baboons, monkeys, warthogs, antelope, birds, and insects." .
