treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:etymology "Genus name Adansonia honors French explorer and botanist Michel Adanson (1727-1806), who wrote the first full botanical description of the species in Senegal. Species name digitata refers to the digits of a hand, describing the palmately compound leaves with typically five (up to nine) leaflets resembling fingers. The common name baobab likely derives from Arabic bu hibab meaning many-seeded fruit, via Medieval Latin bahobab." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_3c83a435-c75d-4efe-8ab1-396396437cc8> a tkp:Insight ;
