treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:fireManagement "Fire ecology: Adapted to fire-prone savanna habitat. Trees >15 years old: Thick bark (5-10cm) provides excellent fire resistance; trees survive most savanna fires. Young trees (<15 years): Vulnerable to fire but can resprout from base after burning. Fruit: Thick woody shells protect seeds from fire temperatures (100-260°C typical, up to 650°C briefly). Management: Allow natural fire regime in savanna; protect young plantings from fire for first 15 years; prescribed burning acceptable in mature stands. Recovery: Bark regenerates even after severe damage; interior can burn out completely while tree survives." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_6494ef4a-ce28-447d-b899-32e7596f1244> a tkp:Insight ;
