treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:flowerColor "White to cream. Large, pendulous, showy flowers up to 20cm (8 inches) diameter. Sweet-scented fragrance, strongest at night. Flowers emerge in late afternoon from large round buds on long drooping stalks (unique to A. digitata among Adansonia species). Flowers open fully at night for bat pollination. Flowers last only 24 hours, then turn brown and fall, developing an unpleasant odor. Flowering period: early summer (October-December in Southern Hemisphere, varies by region)." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_ff3d031f-3eef-447d-b22f-803ec5b20bb8> a tkp:Insight ;
