treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:fruitType "Large, indehiscent capsule (drupe-like). Shape: ovoid to oblong-cylindrical, highly variable. Size: up to 25cm (10 inches) long. Outer shell: hard, woody, 6-10mm thick, covered with yellowish-brown velvety hairs. Inner pulp: dry, powdery, cream-colored, separates into chunks. Seeds: kidney-shaped, black, hard, numerous (dispersed within pulp). Fruit hangs on long stalks (10-90cm). Ripens naturally on tree; only fruit in the world that dries completely on the branch (6 months in sun)." .
