treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:generalDescription "Adansonia digitata is a massive, long-lived deciduous tree native to sub-Saharan African savannas and the southern Arabian Peninsula. Known as the Tree of Life, it is characterized by its enormously swollen, water-storing trunk that can reach 25m in height and 10-14m in diameter. The tree is leafless for about 8 months of the year and produces large, pendulous white flowers pollinated by fruit bats. Its hard-shelled fruit contains a nutritious powdery pulp exceptionally rich in vitamin C. The species is a keystone ecosystem engineer, providing food, water, and shelter for numerous wildlife species." .
