treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:growthForm "Massive deciduous pachycaul tree. Single- or multi-stemmed with hugely swollen, bottle-shaped trunk (caudiciform growth). Typically 15-25m tall, occasionally to 30m. Trunk diameter commonly 5-10m, exceptionally up to 14m; circumference can exceed 20m. Sparse, spreading crown with thick, tapering branches resembling roots. Hollow trunk formation common in large specimens, created by fusion of 3-8 stems sprouting from roots rather than decay. Slow-growing but very long-lived." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_db8d57cc-1834-4f0c-be53-9f59cad41a2c> a tkp:Insight ;
