treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:leafType "Palmately compound (digitate) with 5-7 (sometimes up to 9) leaflets arranged like fingers of a hand. Leaflets: obovate to elliptic, 5-15cm long, entire margins. Young leaves and regenerating shoots may have simple leaves; transition to compound leaves occurs with maturity. Deciduous: leaves shed at start of dry season, tree leafless for approximately 8 months. Foliage appears following first rains. Young leaves edible and harvested for human consumption." .
