treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:lifespan "Typically 1,000-1,500 years. Exceptional specimens reach 2,000+ years. Radiocarbon-dated specimens: Panke baobab (Zimbabwe) ~2,450 years old (oldest documented angiosperm when it died in 2011); Dorslandboom (Namibia) and Glencoe (South Africa) ~2,000 years; Grootboom ~1,275 years. A 7m diameter tree is approximately 600 years old. Longevity possibly enhanced by ability to sprout new stems periodically." .
<https://treekipedia.silvi.earth/ontology#insight_3a20fed1-a54e-489f-8d43-d334f90c2d7a> a tkp:Insight ;
