treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:maximumDiameter "Trunk diameter commonly 5-10 meters (16-33 feet). Maximum reported: up to 14 meters (46 feet) diameter. Circumference can exceed 20 meters (65 feet). The Sunland Baobab in South Africa had a circumference of 33 meters before partial collapse. Trunk size correlates with water storage capacity rather than age alone." .
