treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:maximumTreeAge "Oldest confirmed specimen: Panke baobab in Zimbabwe, radiocarbon-dated to approximately 2,450 years old at time of death in 2011—the oldest documented angiosperm (flowering plant). Other very old specimens: Dorslandboom (Namibia) ~2,000 years, Glencoe (South Africa) ~2,000 years, Platland/Sunland baobab stems 750-1,060 years. Many of the largest, oldest baobabs have died in the early 21st century from unknown causes." .
