treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:nativeHabitats "Native to sub-Saharan Africa: from Mauritania and Senegal (west) to Sudan and Eritrea (northeast), south through East Africa to South Africa, Namibia, and Botswana. Also native to southern Arabian Peninsula (Yemen, Oman). Introduced and naturalized in: Comoros, Madagascar, Indian subcontinent (India, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh), Vietnam, Mozambique Channel islands. Adapted to tropical semi-arid climates with pronounced dry seasons (4-10 months). Köppen climate zones: Aw (tropical savanna), BSh (hot semi-arid)." .
