treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:nonTimberProducts "Bark fiber: Strong, durable; used for rope, cordage, baskets, cloth, musical instrument strings, waterproof hats. Bark regenerates after harvest. Leaves: Edible (cooked as vegetable, dried and powdered); livestock fodder; traditional medicine. Fruit pulp: Nutritious powder (superfood export); traditional beverages; food additive. Seeds: Edible roasted; pressed for oil (cosmetics, cooking); traditional medicine. Flowers: Edible; nectar harvested. Roots: Young roots edible; traditional medicine. Gum: Adhesive applications. Pollen: Glue. Tannins: From bark and pulp for tanning leather and coagulating rubber." .
