treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:nutritional_caloric_value "Fruit pulp (per 100g): Vitamin C 175-466mg (7-10x oranges, varies by location); Fiber ~47g (50% of dry weight, 2/3 soluble prebiotic, 1/3 insoluble); Potassium 1000-2000mg; Calcium 285-375mg; Magnesium ~160mg; Protein 2-3g. Antioxidant content: Highest of any whole fruit. Seeds: Rich in lysine, thiamine, calcium, iron; oil contains oleic and linoleic fatty acids. Leaves: Good source of protein, calcium, iron, vitamin A when cooked. Gluten-free. Energy: Moderate carbohydrate content. Commercial powder: ~46.9g fiber, 266mg vitamin C per 100g. Designated superfood; approved for food use by FDA and EU." .
