treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:plantingRecipes "Seed collection: Harvest ripe fruit; extract seeds from dry pulp. Scarification required (hard seed coat): Hot water soak (24-48 hours) + mechanical scarification, OR concentrated sulfuric acid (98%) for 6-24 hours (most effective), OR passage through animal gut (elephant digestion). Sowing: Plant 2-6cm deep in sandy, well-draining medium. Temperature: Maintain >24°C for germination. Germination time: 2-6 weeks with treatment, months-years without. Transplanting: Handle carefully (sensitive taproot). Frost protection: Critical for young trees; bring indoors in winter in marginal climates. Grafting: Mature scions can induce early fruiting (20 months post-transplant)." .
