treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:propagation_methods "Sexual (seed): Primary method; requires scarification due to hard seed coat. Best treatments: sulfuric acid (6-24 hours) or hot water + mechanical scarification. Germination improved by passage through elephant/baboon digestive tract. Highest germination in sandy soil (75%). Vegetative: Root cuttings possible; grafting and budding successful. Grafting mature scions onto seedlings induces very early fruiting (20 months). In vitro: Tissue culture protocols developed. Natural regeneration: Often poor due to seed predation and seedling browsing; fire kills ungerminated seeds not protected by fruit shell." .
