treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:stewardshipPractices "Protection: Designate as heritage/protected trees; restrict development in baobab areas. Sustainable harvesting: Limit bark removal to <50% circumference with multi-year recovery periods; regulate fruit collection to prevent over-harvesting; promote tenure systems (private/communal) over state control for better stewardship. Planting: Use pre-treated seeds or vegetative propagation; provide frost protection for young trees; ensure good drainage. Water: Avoid irrigation once established (causes rot); protect from waterlogging. Fire management: Allow natural fire regime; protect young trees (<15 years) from fire damage." .
