treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:timberValue "Wood: Soft, spongy, lightweight (density 0.28-0.32 tonnes/m³; air-dried 320 kg/m³). Color: Whitish. Durability: Low; susceptible to rot if exposed to moisture. Commercial timber value: Very low; not used for structural lumber. Uses: Canoes, rafts, fishing net floats, wooden platters and trays, boxes, insulating boards. Special value: Hollow trunks used as water cisterns (400-8,000+ liters capacity), shelters, storage, even chapels and shops. Comparative: Similar to other Bombacaceae; used only where light, low-quality timber acceptable. Primary value is in living tree services, not harvested timber." .
