treekipedia:AngMaMaMlVc33502-00 tkp:tolerances "Drought: Exceptional tolerance; trunk stores 4,000-120,000+ liters of water. Fire: Excellent tolerance; thick (5-10cm) fire-resistant bark protects mature trees (>15 years); young trees can resprout after fire; fruit shells also fire-resistant. Termites: Resistant. Salt: Low tolerance. Wind: Good tolerance due to massive trunk and flexible branches. Flooding/Waterlogging: Very poor tolerance; highly sensitive. Frost: No tolerance; kills trees. Poor soil: Good tolerance of nutrient-deficient conditions." .
